course: dictionary
lesson: 5181
title: Itch: a feeling and a wish
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An itch is a feeling on your skin that makes you want to scratch it. You can also say your skin itches, or that a jumper itches when the wool feels scratchy. «Some hairy caterpillars have tiny hairs that break off and make skin itch and burn» tells you that something touching the skin can cause an itch.
explain: Itch can also show a wish. «Itching to» means you really want to do something soon, as in «itching to go». So when you meet itch, ask yourself: is this about skin, or about wanting something? The words around it give the clue.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Hay fever causes sneezing, itching and a runny nose» fits the skin meaning, because a runny nose and sneezing are body feelings. «The children were itching to open their presents» fits the wish meaning, because they wanted to open them soon.
fact: An itch is a feeling on the skin that makes you want to scratch.
fact: Itch can be a noun (an itch) or a verb (your skin itches).
fact: Insect bites, nettles, dry skin and chickenpox can all make you itch.
fact: Scratching can break the skin and let germs in, so a cool cloth or cream is often better.
fact: «Itchy feet» means wanting to travel.
exercise: «Hay fever causes sneezing, itching and a runny nose.» What is itching here? | Wanting to do something very soon | *A feeling on the skin that makes you want to scratch | A soft woolly jumper | Feeling very tired
exercise: Ella says, «I'm itching to open my present!» What does itching mean? | *Wanting very much to do it soon | Being scared of the box | Feeling a rash on her skin | Covered in wool
exercise: «Some hairy caterpillars have tiny hairs that make skin itch and burn.» Find and copy one word that names a feeling on the skin. | nests | *itch | silky | hairy
test: «When the Rhino buttons it back on, it itches so badly that he rubs against the palm tree.» What does itches mean here? | Is very cold | Is sewn with buttons | *Feels like it needs scratching | Shines brightly
test: Dad says, «My new jumper itches.» What does this mean? | I want to go out soon | My jumper is too big | *The wool feels scratchy on my skin | The jumper is wet
exam: Mia says «itchy feet» means her feet are sore. Who is right? | Mia is right, because itchy feet means cold toes | *Mia is wrong, because itchy feet means wanting to travel | Mia is wrong, because itchy feet means dancing | Mia is right, because her feet are sore
